Subject: [PATCH] Admit request steering and isolate prefix cache identity

Replay baseline: r6x author head 7316c7f9fae1bc4a0b7ab1848de0db4143eec5d2 and preceding
0500-series downstream patches. The original base and validation entries
below are historical provenance; r6x qualification is recorded separately.

Base: r6v plus profile contracts. Rationale: canonical FP32 request dose and content-bound cache salt before scheduling. Stock requests retain their original salt and optional dependencies stay unloaded. Quality: reject unsupported resumable identity changes. Validation: CPU request, boundary and salt tests; real prefix matching remains an integration gate. Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; no upstream submission.
